  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Cybersecurity Data**\n\nI\'m now generating synthetic cybersecurity data to populate `src/data/cyberData.ts`. The focus is on creating 18 interconnected nodes across various tiers. I\'ve begun to define the perimeter/ingress nodes, starting with Internet Gateway, NextGen WAF/Edge Firewall, and Global Load Balancer. I\'ll continue to flesh out the remaining nodes and their relationships.\n\n\n**Defining Node Connections**\n\nI\'ve expanded the node definitions, now including the DMZ Reverse Proxy as an ingress point. Application and cloud clusters are next on my list, specifically Kubernetes clusters on AWS and GCP, alongside a Payment Processing API Gateway and the Auth & IAM directory. I\'m also planning the internal microservices mesh. The focus continues to be on core data and storage, plus operations, management, and endpoint nodes, ensuring interconnected data flows and realistic threat signals.\n\n\n"
