  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Build the complete application shell and integrate the 3D viewer.** (IMPLEMENTATION)\n  - The user requested a \"complete, production-ready, responsive web application\" with a \"consistent shell\" and specific pages (Dashboard, Infrastructure, Assets, etc.).\n- **Implement the remaining pages and navigation.** (NOT STARTED)\n  - The application structure requires pages for `/dashboard`, `/infrastructure`, `/assets`, `/detections`, `/investigations`, `/risk-quantification`, `/threat-intelligence`, `/recommendations`, `/reports`, and `/settings`.\n- **Finalize responsive design and accessibility.** (NOT STARTED)\n  - Ensure the application is fully responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile, and meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards.\n- **Implement real-time updates and backend integration.** (NOT STARTED)\n  - The user requested support for real-time updates (WebSockets/SSE) and clean backend integration.\n- **Implement testing and CI/CD.** (NOT STARTED)\n  - The user requested unit, integration, and E2E tests, along with a CI/CD pipeline.\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- The user provided a comprehensive \"MASTER PROMPT\" defining the product direction, design philosophy, 3D model specifications, and technical requirements.\n- **Design Philosophy:** \"Premium, modern, intelligent, minimal but information-rich, dark, cinematic, and technically sophisticated.\"\n- **3D Hero Experience:** The 3D model must be the \"visual centerpiece\" and \"hero experience,\" occupying 50\342\200\22365% of the hero visual area on desktop.\n- **Accessibility:** Must be WCAG 2.1 AA compliant, with a non-visual equivalent (2D map) for the 3D viewer.\n- **Data:** Use synthetic data for demonstrations; clearly distinguish it from live integrations.\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Foundation & Infrastructure:**\n  - Initialized project with necessary dependencies (`three`, `@types/three`, `lucide-react`, `motion`).\n  - Configured `metadata.json` and `index.html` with appropriate metadata and fonts (Plus Jakarta Sans, JetBrains Mono).\n  - Enhanced `index.css` with a dark, premium cybersecurity color palette and subtle UI effects.\n- **Data Layer:**\n  - Defined comprehensive TypeScript interfaces in `src/types/index.ts` covering infrastructure nodes, vulnerabilities, data flows, anomalies, investigations, recommendations, and enterprise risk metrics.\n  - Created `src/data/cyberData.ts` with realistic synthetic cybersecurity data.\n  - Implemented `src/services/apiService.ts` to manage application state and emulate REST API endpoints.\n- **3D Components:**\n  - Created `src/components/three/ThreeInfrastructureViewer.tsx`: The main 3D viewer component using Three.js, implementing camera controls, raycasting for node selection, data flow animations, and label projection.\n  - Created `src/components/three/ViewerControls.tsx`: UI controls for the 3D viewer (rotation, zoom, quality, overlays).\n  - Created `src/components/three/AssetDetailPanel.tsx`: A detailed panel for inspecting selected assets, including risk scores, vulnerabilities, and telemetry.\n  - Created `src/components/three/TwoDTopologyFallback.tsx`: A fully functional 2D SVG-based fallback for the 3D viewer, ensuring accessibility and compatibility.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:** The application uses a React-based architecture with a centralized `apiService` for state management. The 3D viewer is built using native Three.js within a `useEffect` hook to manage the WebGL lifecycle, avoiding unnecessary React re-renders.\n- **3D Implementation:** The viewer uses `PerspectiveCamera` with `Spherical` coordinates for OrbitControls-like behavior. Node selection is handled via `Raycaster`. Data flows are rendered as `CatmullRomCurve3` paths with animated `SphereGeometry` packets.\n- **Performance:** The viewer includes a quality selector (`auto`, `high`, `medium`, `low`) to adjust rendering fidelity and pixel ratio based on device capability.\n- **Failures/Constraints:** The 3D viewer is designed to gracefully degrade to a 2D SVG map if WebGL is unavailable or if the user prefers a 2D view.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/metadata.json`: Set app name and description.\n  - `/index.html`: Updated title, meta tags, and added font links.\n  - `/src/index.css`: Added custom CSS for typography, scrollbars, and animations.\n- **Created Files:**\n  - `/src/types/index.ts`: Core data models.\n  - `/src/data/cyberData.ts`: Synthetic datasets.\n  - `/src/services/apiService.ts`: API service layer.\n  - `/src/components/three/TwoDTopologyFallback.tsx`: 2D SVG map component.\n  - `/src/components/three/ViewerControls.tsx`: 3D viewer control UI.\n  - `/src/components/three/AssetDetailPanel.tsx`: Asset detail panel component.\n  - `/src/components/three/ThreeInfrastructureViewer.tsx`: Main 3D viewer component.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/package.json`: Checked dependencies.\n  - `/index.html`: Verified structure.\n  - `/src/index.css`: Verified styles.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Work:** The foundation and 3D viewer components are complete.\n- **Next Steps:**\n  - The next agent should focus on implementing `src/App.tsx` to create the application shell (Layout, Sidebar, TopNavigation).\n  - Integrate the `ThreeInfrastructureViewer` into the main dashboard or infrastructure page within `App.tsx`.\n  - Implement routing to support the pages defined in the \"Application Structure\" section of the master prompt.\n  - Use `lucide-react` for navigation icons and build a responsive sidebar/drawer."
    included_step_index_end: 31
