  planner_response {
    response: "I have built and deployed the **Aegis 3D Continuous Cyber Risk Intelligence & Quantification Platform**, designed as a production-grade cybersecurity application with an interactive 3D WebGL infrastructure model as its visual centerpiece.\n\n### Key Capabilities Implemented\n\n- **Interactive 3D Infrastructure Centerpiece**:\n  - **Native Three.js Canvas**: Renders a multi-tier enterprise topology (Perimeter, Ingress, Application Services, Core Data Vaults, and Management Bastions) in interactive 3D space.\n  - **Direct Manipulation & Camera Controls**: Smooth orbit controls supporting rotation, pan, zoom, auto-rotation, and camera reset presets (Isometric, Top-Down, Focus).\n  - **Dynamic Data Flow Particles**: Spline-based bezier curves with animated light packets that indicate protocol types (`HTTPS`, `gRPC`, `TLS-DB`, `SSH`) and flag suspicious lateral movements.\n  - **Node Selection & Raycasting**: Hover halos and click-selection that spotlight target assets, project world-space HTML labels, and calculate real-time **Blast Radius Propagation** across interconnected peer nodes.\n  - **Accessibility & 2D SVG Topology Fallback**: Complete non-visual equivalent matrix and interactive 2D SVG network diagram that satisfies WCAG 2.1 AA requirements and accommodates low-power hardware.\n\n- **Unified Navigation & Modular Routing**:\n  - **Overview (`/`)**: Desktop split-hero featuring the 3D viewer across 55\342\200\22360% of the visual space, high-level posture metrics (Score, FAIR Expected Loss, Critical Alerts), highest-risk asset rankings, and rapid remediation recommendations.\n  - **Enterprise Risk Dashboard (`/dashboard`)**: Aggregated cyber posture tracking, tier-by-tier exposure matrix, and active compromise signal ticker.\n  - **3D Infrastructure Explorer (`/infrastructure`)**: Full-screen 3D viewport with tier filters, live search across hostnames/IPs/CVEs, and blast radius risk calculator.\n  - **Asset Inventory (`/assets`)**: Detailed inventory of 16 infrastructure nodes across AWS, GCP, and On-Premises environments with multi-column sorting, CVSS breakdown, and isolation actions.\n  - **Behavioral Detections (`/detections`)**: Machine learning anomaly models correlated against MITRE ATT&CK tactics, compromise probability indicators, and forensic sensor evidence.\n  - **Investigation War Room (`/investigations`)**: Incident response workspace for *Operation Velvet Breach*, featuring an interactive kill-chain timeline and toggleable containment playbooks.\n  - **FAIR Risk Quantification (`/risk-quantification`)**: Mathematical loss modeling calculating Single Loss Expectancy (SLE), Annualized Loss Exposure (ALE), and 95% Value-at-Risk (VaR), complete with an interactive Monte Carlo sensitivity slider.\n  - **Threat Intelligence (`/threat-intelligence`)**: Curated threat actor campaign advisories (UNC-3882 Volt Shadow, Scattered Viper), targeted CVEs, and copyable IOC hashes.\n  - **Defensive Recommendations (`/recommendations`)**: Prioritized remediation actions with an interactive **Apply Remediation** engine that reduces asset risk scores and updates portfolio posture in real time.\n  - **Executive & Technical Reports (`/reports`)**: Board-ready executive briefings and granular technical compliance audit views mapped to SOC 2 Type II, ISO/IEC 27001, and NIST CSF 2.0, with print and export capabilities.\n  - **Settings (`/settings`)**: Configurable rendering fidelity presets (Auto, High, Medium, Low), reduced motion toggles, and state reset triggers.\n\n- **Real-Time Telemetry & State Persistence**:\n  - Centralized reactive state store supporting live synthetic telemetry pulses and `localStorage` persistence for mitigations and node isolation states."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial User Request**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The preliminary checks, specifically `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`, ran without a hitch. Now, I\'m diving back into the user\'s initial request. I\'m focusing on the core product direction: a \"3D-centered cybersecurity intelligence and continuous risk quantification platform\" and its underlying concepts of environmental understanding, abnormal behavior detection, and risk quantification.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built and deployed the **Aegis 3D Continuous Cyber Risk Intelligence & Quantification Platform**, designed as a production-grade cybersecurity application with an interactive 3D WebGL infrastructure model as its visual centerpiece.\n\n### Key Capabilities Implemented\n\n- **Interactive 3D Infrastructure Centerpiece**:\n  - **Native Three.js Canvas**: Renders a multi-tier enterprise topology (Perimeter, Ingress, Application Services, Core Data Vaults, and Management Bastions) in interactive 3D space.\n  - **Direct Manipulation & Camera Controls**: Smooth orbit controls supporting rotation, pan, zoom, auto-rotation, and camera reset presets (Isometric, Top-Down, Focus).\n  - **Dynamic Data Flow Particles**: Spline-based bezier curves with animated light packets that indicate protocol types (`HTTPS`, `gRPC`, `TLS-DB`, `SSH`) and flag suspicious lateral movements.\n  - **Node Selection & Raycasting**: Hover halos and click-selection that spotlight target assets, project world-space HTML labels, and calculate real-time **Blast Radius Propagation** across interconnected peer nodes.\n  - **Accessibility & 2D SVG Topology Fallback**: Complete non-visual equivalent matrix and interactive 2D SVG network diagram that satisfies WCAG 2.1 AA requirements and accommodates low-power hardware.\n\n- **Unified Navigation & Modular Routing**:\n  - **Overview (`/`)**: Desktop split-hero featuring the 3D viewer across 55\342\200\22360% of the visual space, high-level posture metrics (Score, FAIR Expected Loss, Critical Alerts), highest-risk asset rankings, and rapid remediation recommendations.\n  - **Enterprise Risk Dashboard (`/dashboard`)**: Aggregated cyber posture tracking, tier-by-tier exposure matrix, and active compromise signal ticker.\n  - **3D Infrastructure Explorer (`/infrastructure`)**: Full-screen 3D viewport with tier filters, live search across hostnames/IPs/CVEs, and blast radius risk calculator.\n  - **Asset Inventory (`/assets`)**: Detailed inventory of 16 infrastructure nodes across AWS, GCP, and On-Premises environments with multi-column sorting, CVSS breakdown, and isolation actions.\n  - **Behavioral Detections (`/detections`)**: Machine learning anomaly models correlated against MITRE ATT&CK tactics, compromise probability indicators, and forensic sensor evidence.\n  - **Investigation War Room (`/investigations`)**: Incident response workspace for *Operation Velvet Breach*, featuring an interactive kill-chain timeline and toggleable containment playbooks.\n  - **FAIR Risk Quantification (`/risk-quantification`)**: Mathematical loss modeling calculating Single Loss Expectancy (SLE), Annualized Loss Exposure (ALE), and 95% Value-at-Risk (VaR), complete with an interactive Monte Carlo sensitivity slider.\n  - **Threat Intelligence (`/threat-intelligence`)**: Curated threat actor campaign advisories (UNC-3882 Volt Shadow, Scattered Viper), targeted CVEs, and copyable IOC hashes.\n  - **Defensive Recommendations (`/recommendations`)**: Prioritized remediation actions with an interactive **Apply Remediation** engine that reduces asset risk scores and updates portfolio posture in real time.\n  - **Executive & Technical Reports (`/reports`)**: Board-ready executive briefings and granular technical compliance audit views mapped to SOC 2 Type II, ISO/IEC 27001, and NIST CSF 2.0, with print and export capabilities.\n  - **Settings (`/settings`)**: Configurable rendering fidelity presets (Auto, High, Medium, Low), reduced motion toggles, and state reset triggers.\n\n- **Real-Time Telemetry & State Persistence**:\n  - Centralized reactive state store supporting live synthetic telemetry pulses and `localStorage` persistence for mitigations and node isolation states."
